    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into the July 23 slate with a condensed active roster, leaving our primary offensive engine\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014idle today due to team off-days. With fewer bodies available, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** anchors the lineup with the day\u2019s premier score of 67.10. His matchup against Legumina is favorable; the 4.32 xERA suggests a prime opportunity for extra-base hits, and the favorable park shift combined with an advantageous #2 spot in the order elevates his production floor significantly. **Drake Baldwin** follows as our secondary point of interest at 59.15, benefitting heavily from a leadoff assignment that bolsters his daily efficiency score despite facing the left-handed Hart.\n\nWhile **Brayan Rocchio** (44.53) and **Dominic Smith** (40.68) round out the starters, both are operating near the lower threshold of our efficiency model. **Brayan Rocchio** faces a stiff challenge against Bradley, T, whose 3.82 xERA acts as a drag on his raw projection, while **Dominic Smith** is hampered by a L/L platoon disadvantage that suppresses his overall utility. We narrowly considered **Jackson Merrill** for an active role, but the combination of a daunting matchup against Sale\u2014who carries a restrictive 3.14 xERA\u2014and the inefficiency of the L/L platoon split made the bench the mathematically sound decision for his health and our game cap management.\n\nInvestors should monitor the weather closely for the **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** matchup; any late-breaking precipitation could jeopardize their scoring potential, as their current \"Strong/Marginal\" status relies on steady park conditions. We are maintaining a conservative posture with our bench depth\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos**\u2014as we prioritize preserving our games-played allocation for higher-leverage matchups later in the week. By keeping **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Jacob Wilson** in reserve, we ensure that we aren't burning cap space on mid-tier matchups, allowing us to pivot to the full strength of our roster once **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, and the rest of our prospect contingent return to consistent high-leverage roles.",
